U5 test262 shard cold/warm series
=================================

Host: Linux workstation, 16 CPUs, 61 GiB. Target linux-x86_64-gnu.
Command per arm: mise run test:test262 --shard 1/10
ZIG_GLOBAL_CACHE_DIR=/data/zig-cache/m5ci-zig-cache-share throughout.
XDG_CACHE_HOME pointed at a probe directory so the runtime archive stayed
warm (as the CI cache action leaves it) while the harness object directory
was removed before every arm (as CI never restores one).
A cold arm emptied the Zig cache directory first; a warm arm kept it.
A competing gate ran on the host throughout; load averages are recorded.

new-o-entries counts directories present after the arm but not before.
cache-bytes-kib is du -sk of the whole cache directory.

